  </metadata>
  <prompt>Deliver FR-B3/B5 as a TRUE grounded suggestion turn (Option B, owner-approved 2026-08-06): on a tab's first open, run ONE grounded agent turn — server-side, deterministically pre-filtered to Bindings whose ContextTypeTags include the tab's contextType — that reads the active-tab compact content and SELECTS + PHRASES ≤3 content-specific follow-on chips. Cache per tabId (fire at most once per tab; never on switch-back). Render via the reactive useConsumerChips surface. NOT a static per-type menu; NOT a classifier; NOT a SprkChat fork; NOT a second dispatch protocol.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Full-stack: .NET Minimal API + the SprkChat agent-turn/dispatch infra (BFF) AND React/TypeScript + Fluent v9 (SpaarkeAi). Disciplined about ADR-039 (one grounded decider, deterministic pre-filter only), ADR-040 (store-before-render), and reusing — not resurrecting/forking — existing surfaces.</role>
  <goal>Opening a content-rich tab fires exactly ONE grounded suggestion turn whose ≤3 chips are specific to THAT tab's content (an NDA tab ≠ an invoice tab ≠ a generic "document" menu); switching away and back fires zero additional turns; chips render via useConsumerChips and are dismissible; no generic boilerplate chips on content-rich tabs.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>
      Owner chose Option B over a deterministic catalog filter because A is structurally a context-type-keyed STATIC menu (same chips for every document tab) and therefore CANNOT satisfy FR-B5 ("generic boilerplate chips are not emitted for content-rich tabs"). B is the product capability: the Assistant reads what you opened and proposes the right next moves for it. See notes/deviations.md §"Task 022 Option B".

      Verified structural gaps this design closes (from the 022 exploration):
      1. `CapabilityDto` (CapabilityDiscoveryEndpoints.cs:177-183) does NOT expose ContextTypeTags — so contextType filtering CANNOT be client-side; it is done SERVER-SIDE in the suggest path (which reads Binding.ContextTypeTags via ConsumerRoutingService — task 021, already present).
      2. No server path consumes activeContext.contextType and no client "fire a grounded turn on tab-open" handle exists — this task adds the purpose-built suggest endpoint + the client trigger.

      Client seam ALREADY MAPPED (reuse, don't re-derive):
      - Trigger: the existing `usePaneEvent("workspace", …)` subscriber at ConversationPane.tsx:2331; `deriveActiveTabFocusStamp(event)` (activeTabFocusStamp.ts:57-67) returns `{ widgetType, contextType, tabId, displayName, compactState }`. `focusStamp.tabId` + `focusStamp.contextType` are your trigger data.
      - Once-per-tab idiom to mirror: `wizardAutoRunHandledRef = useRef<Set<string>>(new Set())` (ConversationPane.tsx:596) guarded via `.has(k)/.add(k)`.
      - Render seam: `chips.acceptChips(rawChips)` (useConsumerChips.tsx:550-561; controller wired at ConversationPane.tsx:799-872, rendered via `chips.consumerChipsSlot` in `transcriptFooter` at :2472). acceptChips replaces-only-when-non-empty and does NOT cap — the caller slices to ≤3. Chip wire shape: `{ targetBindingId|target_binding_id, label|chip_label, args|prefillSlots }` (parseConsumerChips).
      - `activeContext` compact tab state is already stamped onto outbound bodies (ConversationPane.tsx:1929-1931) and typed server-side as ChatActiveContext (task 012, ChatEndpoints.cs) — reuse this shape for the suggest request.
      - `useSuggestionCards` is DELETED (confirmed). `SuggestionCard.tsx` is retained/presentational — do NOT re-wire it (de-facto resurrection).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Ai/ChatEndpoints.cs (ChatActiveContext DTO + session message endpoints; add POST …/{id}/suggest here or a sibling SuggestionEndpoints.cs)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Chat/SprkChatAgentFactory.cs (grounded agent-turn construction — reuse for the suggestion turn)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/ConsumerRoutingService.cs (deterministic candidate resolution; add a contextType pre-filter over Binding.ContextTypeTags from task 021)</file>
      <file>src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/ConversationPane.tsx (tab-open trigger + once-per-tab cache + acceptChips render)</file>
      <file>src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/useConsumerChips.tsx (render seam — acceptChips; do NOT add contextType logic here)</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/events/PaneEventTypes.ts (active_widget_changed payload: tabId :445, widgetContextType :440)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-039">EXACTLY ONE grounded decider. The contextType→ContextTypeTags narrowing is a DETERMINISTIC PRE-FILTER (permitted). The ONE grounded turn then selects/phrases ≤3 chips. MUST NOT add a classifier/reranker/keyword map, a SECOND intent mechanism, or a SECOND dispatch protocol. The suggestion turn rides the existing single dispatch surface — no new routing contract.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-040">Store-before-render: any tool reads the suggestion turn consumes get citations + ledger persistence per the existing turn path. Do NOT invent a new persistence store. If a chip-only suggestion output cannot be ledgered within the existing StoredSession model, STOP and escalate (do not add a store).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">The active-tab compact content passed to the suggest turn is the SAME bounded compact-ambient shape already permitted (Path A). Do NOT widen it; do NOT dump full content (full body stays on-demand via eml-render, FR-C4).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Render via the REACTIVE surface (useConsumerChips / chips.acceptChips). MUST NOT reuse or resurrect useSuggestionCards or re-wire SuggestionCard.tsx.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Seam rule — MUST NOT fork SprkChat. Client fires the suggest call imperatively (fetch), feeds chips via acceptChips; the outbound-body/decorate seam is unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">NFR-02 — fire AT MOST once per tab (cache by tabId; Set&lt;string&gt; ref). Never on switch-back. ≤3 chips, dismissible, non-modal. No generic boilerplate on content-rich tabs.</constraint>
    <constraint source="BFF-§10">New endpoint + service on the BFF. State Placement Justification (load bff-extensions.md). Publish ≤60 MB (baseline ~48.25 MB); report absolute + delta. No new NuGet packages expected. Add/adjust tests per the test-update obligation.</constraint>
  </constraints>
