  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">BFF deterministic pre-filter: add a contextType filter over candidate Bindings in ConsumerRoutingService (reuse Binding.ContextTypeTags from task 021; a Binding matches when its tags contain the requested contextType OR its tags are empty=any). This is the ADR-039 permitted pre-filter — no ranking, no model call.</step>
    <step order="2">BFF suggestion service: run ONE grounded agent turn (reuse SprkChatAgentFactory / the existing agent-turn infra — do NOT fork it) that receives the active-tab compact content + the pre-filtered candidate capabilities (bindingId + tool-description/label) and returns ≤3 CONTENT-SPECIFIC chips it selected + phrased. Structured output {targetBindingId, label, args?}, capped at 3. Ledger/cite per the existing turn path (ADR-040). Escalate rather than fork/duplicate if the existing turn infra can't yield a chip-only output cleanly.</step>
    <step order="3">BFF endpoint: POST /api/ai/chat/sessions/{sessionId}/suggest — request { contextType, activeContext } (reuse ChatActiveContext), returns { chips: ≤3 }. Do NOT inject a transcript/Assistant message (silent proactive suggestion). Register DI; RequireAuthorization; add a contract/integration test.</step>
    <step order="4">BFF build (dotnet build) + tests + publish-size check + deploy (Deploy-BffApi.ps1); report size + delta; /healthz.</step>
    <step order="5">Client trigger: in the existing `usePaneEvent("workspace", …)` handler (ConversationPane.tsx:2331), when a focusStamp with a tabId+contextType arrives for a not-yet-suggested tab (Set&lt;string&gt; ref like wizardAutoRunHandledRef), call POST /suggest ONCE, cache the ≤3 chips per tabId, and render via chips.acceptChips(sliced≤3). No re-fire on switch-back. (Optional: restore cached chips on switch-back.)</step>
    <step order="6">Client build (npm run typecheck — Surface-owned: 0) + seam test: two active_widget_changed with same tabId ⇒ suggest called once; different tabId ⇒ called again; ≤3 chips reach acceptChips. Model on useConsumerChips.surface-launch.test.tsx + ConversationPane.active-context-decorate.e2e.test.tsx.</step>
    <step order="7">Deploy SpaarkeAi code page (Deploy-SpaarkeAi.ps1, clear Vite cache first). Update TASK-INDEX ✅ + current-task + notes.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a chip-only grounded suggestion output cannot be produced by reusing the existing agent-turn infra WITHOUT forking SprkChat or adding a second dispatch protocol/routing contract, STOP and escalate (ADR-039).</trigger>
    <trigger>If ledgering the suggestion turn (ADR-040 store-before-render) would require a new persistence store or a change to the StoredSession model's identity, STOP and escalate.</trigger>
    <trigger>If BFF publish delta ≥+5 MB or cumulative ≥55 MB, STOP and escalate per BFF §10 before deploying.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Content-specific, once per tab">
      <steps>Open a content-rich document/email tab; verify ≤3 chips that are SPECIFIC to that content (not a generic per-type menu) and exactly one suggest call fires. Switch away and back; verify zero additional suggest calls. Verify chips are dismissible. Include an ADR-021 dark-mode no-regression check.</steps>
      <expected>≤3 content-specific dismissible chips on first open; exactly one suggest call; zero additional on switch-back; no dark-mode regressions.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>
  <justification>
    <existing>ConsumerRoutingService resolves candidate Bindings (has ContextTypeTags from 021); SprkChatAgentFactory runs grounded turns; useConsumerChips renders chips; ChatActiveContext carries compact tab state.</existing>
    <extension>Extend — a contextType pre-filter + a suggest endpoint that REUSES the grounded-turn infra; a client trigger that REUSES the existing focus-stamp subscriber + chip render seam. No new registry, no new dispatch protocol, no SprkChat fork.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without the server suggest path the Assistant cannot offer content-specific proactive chips (FR-B5 fails — only generic per-type menus are possible client-side); FR-B3's grounded, contextType-scoped suggestion has no home.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Ai/ChatEndpoints.cs (or new SuggestionEndpoints.cs)</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Chat/ (suggestion service)</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/ConsumerRoutingService.cs (contextType pre-filter)</output>
    <output type="code">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/ConversationPane.tsx</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Opening a content-rich tab fires exactly one grounded suggest call; the ≤3 chips are specific to that tab's content (verified: different content → different chips, not a fixed per-type menu).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Switch-away-and-back fires zero additional suggest calls (cache keyed by tabId).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">≤3 dismissible chips render via useConsumerChips (NOT useSuggestionCards; SuggestionCard.tsx untouched).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">contextType filtering is a deterministic server-side pre-filter over Binding.ContextTypeTags; the ONE grounded turn is the only decider (no classifier/second mechanism/second dispatch protocol; no SprkChat fork).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No generic boilerplate chips on content-rich tabs.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF builds + tests pass; publish ≤60 MB (absolute + delta reported); both BFF + code page deployed; /healthz 200.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Seam test passes (one fire / zero on switch-back / ≤3 chips).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>Re-scoped STANDARD→FULL, single-file→BFF+client, Option B (owner-approved 2026-08-06). Supersedes the original single-file ConversationPane-only scope. FR-B4 manual refresh = task 023; dev trace = task 024; Reanalyze chip = task 038 (reuses the Reanalyze binding 9c29b488… from 021).</notes>
